'==============================================================================
' Customer Support CRM — user flows (UML activity / state diagrams, PlantUML)
'
' READ-ONLY DOCUMENTATION. Generated from the repository as it stands at
' commit 969bb31 (2026-09-01): the implemented Angular routes and guards, the
' ASP.NET Core controllers and their authorization policies, the Application
' services, the EF Core entities and migrations, and the approved documents in
' docs/ and .squad/.
'
' RULES APPLIED WHILE DRAWING
'   * Nothing here is invented. Every activity corresponds to code that exists.
'   * Anything designed but absent from the code is drawn in red and labelled
'     NOT IMPLEMENTED, with the story that owns it.
'   * Guards hide; they do not protect. Client-side route rules are drawn in
'     the guard lane; the server rule that independently enforces the same
'     thing is drawn in the API lane (architecture.md §2.2, §4.2).
'
' DIAGRAM INDEX (one @startuml block each; the first renders as USER-FLOWS.png)
'   1  USER-FLOWS ............... master: login, authentication, role detection,
'                                 role-based redirect, area map, logout
'   2  USER-FLOWS-authorization . 401 / 403 / 404 / 409 / 422 / 503 branches
'   3  USER-FLOWS-agent ......... Agent lifecycle in the Staff Workspace
'   4  USER-FLOWS-manager ....... Manager lifecycle (cross-department)
'   5  USER-FLOWS-administrator . Administrator lifecycle (Administration)
'   6  USER-FLOWS-customer ...... Customer lifecycle in the Customer Portal
'   7  USER-FLOWS-ticket-state .. UML state machine: the A-5 / A-16 lifecycle
'   8  USER-FLOWS-sla ........... SLA sweep, escalation and notifications
'   9  USER-FLOWS-ai-kb ......... AI assists and Knowledge Base retrieval
'  10  USER-FLOWS-not-implemented inventory of designed-but-absent flows
'==============================================================================

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' 1. MASTER FLOW — login -> authentication -> role detection -> redirect -> areas
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml
title Support CRM — master user flow\nLogin, authentication, role detection, role-based redirect, areas, logout\n(implemented state at commit 969bb31, 2026-09-01)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #33475B
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #33475B
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9E6
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDF0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C8B88A

|#E8F0FE|Browser — Angular SPA|
|#E9F7EF|Router + guards (hide only)|
|#FFF4E5|API — ASP.NET Core (api/v1)|
|#FDEAF1|SQL Server via EF Core|

|Browser — Angular SPA|
start
:User opens the app at any URL;
:GET /api/v1/config/bootstrap  «anonymous»\nproduct name, logo, primary colour,\nlanguages (en, ar), default language;
note right
  ConfigController.GetBootstrap — one of the four
  anonymous endpoints (api-design §4.1). Feeds
  branding + the language switcher before sign-in.
end note

if (JWT held in localStorage\nkey "supportcrm.token" ?) then (yes)
  :GET /api/v1/auth/me\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>;
  |API — ASP.NET Core (api/v1)|
  :CurrentUserMiddleware (AD-15)\nreads the subject claim ONLY —\nrole, department and active status\nare deliberately NOT in the token;
  |SQL Server via EF Core|
  :SELECT Id, Email, DisplayName, Role,\nDepartmentId, CustomerId, IsActive\nFROM Users WHERE Id = subject;
  |API — ASP.NET Core (api/v1)|
  if (user exists AND IsActive ?) then (yes)
    :200 Identity\n{id, email, displayName, role,\n departmentId, customerId};
    |Browser — Angular SPA|
    :AuthStore.setIdentity(...);
  else (no — deleted or deactivated)
    :401 unauthenticated;
    |Browser — Angular SPA|
    :errorInterceptor clears the token\nand the notification badge;
    :Router → /auth/login?returnUrl=<url>;
  endif
else (no token)
  |Router + guards (hide only)|
  :authenticatedGuard / roleRedirectGuard\n→ UrlTree /auth/login?returnUrl=<url>;
endif

|Browser — Angular SPA|
if (identity resolved ?) then (no — sign-in required)
  repeat
    :AuthShell renders /auth/login\n(or /auth/register for a new customer);
    if (existing account ?) then (yes — sign in)
      :POST /api/v1/auth/login\n{email, password};
      |API — ASP.NET Core (api/v1)|
      :AuthService.LoginAsync verifies\nthe stored password hash;
      |SQL Server via EF Core|
      :SELECT Users (case-insensitive e-mail)\nINSERT AuditEntry\n  SignInSucceeded | SignInFailed;
      |API — ASP.NET Core (api/v1)|
      :200 AuthToken {accessToken, user}\nor 401 invalid-credentials;
    else (no — customer self-registration)
      :POST /api/v1/auth/register\n{email, password, displayName, ...};
      |API — ASP.NET Core (api/v1)|
      :AuthService.RegisterAsync (A-15) creates\nUser(role = Customer) + Customer\non the configured default branch;
      |SQL Server via EF Core|
      :INSERT Users, Customers\n(409 user-already-exists if the e-mail is taken);
      |API — ASP.NET Core (api/v1)|
      :201 AuthToken — the new customer is\nsigned in, not bounced to the form;
    endif
    |Browser — Angular SPA|
    :Render the inline error for 401 / 409.\nThe anonymous auth endpoints are excluded\nfrom the interceptor's 401 redirect rule;
  repeat while (credentials accepted ?) is (no) not (yes)
  :AuthStore.setToken() → localStorage\nAuthStore.setIdentity();
endif

|Router + guards (hide only)|
:navigateByUrl(returnUrl or "/");
:roleRedirectGuard reads identity.role\nA-4 hierarchy: Customer < Agent < Manager < Administrator;

if (which role ?) then (Customer)
  :UrlTree → /portal  (PortalShell, lazy chunk)\n→ /portal/requests/new;
  |Browser — Angular SPA|
  :CUSTOMER PORTAL\nSubmit a request · Request detail · Help centre;
  note right
    See USER-FLOWS-customer.
    Portal navigation today: "Submit a request" and "Help".
  end note
elseif (Administrator) then
  :UrlTree → /workspace  (StaffShell, lazy chunk)\n→ /workspace/queue   (UI-2 landing);
  |Browser — Angular SPA|
  :STAFF WORKSPACE\nMy queue · Tickets · Customers ·\nKnowledge · Notifications;
  :ADMINISTRATION (second nav section)\nUsers · Audit log · Configuration ·\nKnowledge authoring · /status health check;
  note right
    An Administrator satisfies the Agent guard (A-4),
    so an Administrator sees BOTH sections, and
    TicketScope is unrestricted across departments.
    See USER-FLOWS-administrator.
  end note
elseif (Manager) then
  :UrlTree → /workspace → /workspace/queue;
  |Browser — Angular SPA|
  :STAFF WORKSPACE — same screens as an Agent,\nbut TicketScope is unrestricted across departments\n(A-2, A-4) and the department filter is enabled;
  :<color:#B71C1C>/workspace/reports — the Manager+ dashboard</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>NOT IMPLEMENTED (story 15). The route does not</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>exist, so the URL falls through to /404</color>;
  note right
    See USER-FLOWS-manager.
  end note
else (Agent)
  :UrlTree → /workspace → /workspace/queue;
  |Browser — Angular SPA|
  :STAFF WORKSPACE\nMy queue · Tickets · Customers ·\nKnowledge · Notifications;
  :TicketScope narrows every ticket read and write\nto the agent's own department;
  note right
    See USER-FLOWS-agent.
  end note
endif

|Browser — Angular SPA|
:Work in the area\n(see the per-role diagrams);

partition "Cross-cutting, on every authenticated screen" {
  :Language switcher en / ar,\ndocument direction ltr / rtl (T2-J);
  :Notification bell — NotificationStore.refresh()\non every navigation; nothing polls (T3-B).\nStaff only: skipped for a Customer session;
}

if (how does the session end ?) then (user signs out)
  :AuthService.logout() — client-side ONLY (AP-8).\nNo logout endpoint exists: discard the token,\nclear the unread badge, navigate to /auth/login;
else (server refuses — 401)
  :errorInterceptor clears the store and\nredirects to /auth/login?returnUrl=<current>;
endif
stop

legend right
  |= Lane |= Meaning |
  | Browser | Angular standalone components, PrimeNG/Sakai shell |
  | Guards | authenticatedGuard, roleAtLeast(...), roleRedirectGuard — they hide only |
  | API | Controllers → Application services; policies RequireCustomer/Agent/Manager/Administrator |
  | SQL Server | EF Core, one unit of work per request, committed once |
  Red text marks what is NOT IMPLEMENTED.
end legend
@enduml

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' 2. AUTHORIZATION — the 401 / 403 / 404 / 409 / 422 / 413 / 503 branches
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml USER-FLOWS-authorization
title Authorization and failure branches — what each refusal means, and where it is decided

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9E6

|#E9F7EF|Angular router + guards|
|#FFF4E5|ASP.NET Core pipeline|
|#E8F0FE|Angular errorInterceptor|

|Angular router + guards|
start
:User navigates to a route;
if (route matches the tree ?) then (no)
  :<color:#B71C1C>wildcard "**" → redirect /404</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>StatusPageComponent(kind = notFound)</color>;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (authenticatedGuard: identity, or a usable token ?) then (no)
  :UrlTree /auth/login?returnUrl=<url>;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (roleAtLeast(minimum) — the A-4 rank ?) then (insufficient)
  :<color:#B71C1C>UrlTree → /403</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>StatusPageComponent(kind = forbidden)</color>;
  note right
    Route rules mirror server rules; they never
    replace them. /workspace needs Agent+,
    /admin and /status need Administrator,
    /portal needs any authenticated user.
  end note
  stop
else (sufficient)
endif

|ASP.NET Core pipeline|
:Request carries the Bearer token\n(authInterceptor attaches it when one is held);
if (JWT valid ?) then (no)
  :<color:#B71C1C>401 — authentication failed</color>;
  detach
else (yes)
endif

:CurrentUserMiddleware re-reads the user row (AD-15);
if (user exists AND IsActive ?) then (no)
  :<color:#B71C1C>401 unauthenticated —</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>a deactivated user is refused HERE, not 403</color>;
  detach
else (yes)
endif

if (endpoint policy satisfied ?\nRequireCustomer / RequireAgent /\nRequireManager / RequireAdministrator) then (no)
  :<color:#B71C1C>403 — a capability denial the caller can</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>infer from their own role</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>(e.g. Customer → GET /config/staff)</color>;
  detach
else (yes)
endif

if (row in the caller's scope ?\nTicketScope / customer ownership / notification owner) then (no)
  :<color:#B71C1C>404 — worded identically to a missing id (AP-4).</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>An out-of-department ticket, another customer's ticket,</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>or an internal / unpublished article on the portal KB</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>endpoints must not be confirmable</color>;
  detach
else (yes)
endif

if (request valid ?) then (no)
  :<color:#B71C1C>400 — validation, unknown member (AP-10),</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>unsupported sort field (AP-15),</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>unknown categoryCode</color>;
  detach
else (yes)
endif

if (which operation ?) then (ticket transition)
  if (A-16 authority — TransitionAuthority.MayInvoke ?) then (permitted)
    if (A-5 edge legal — TicketLifecycle.IsLegal ?) then (legal)
      :200 Ticket (status changed, activity + audit written);
    else (illegal)
      :<color:#B71C1C>409 illegal-transition</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>+ allowedTransitions in the problem detail</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>(the only place the contract publishes the set — F-1)</color>;
    endif
  else (refused)
    :<color:#B71C1C>403 transition-not-permitted</color>;
  endif

elseif (assignment) then
  if (assignee is active staff in the ticket's department ?) then (yes)
    :200 Ticket — status unchanged (A-18);
  else (no)
    :<color:#B71C1C>422 assignee-out-of-department</color>;
  endif

elseif (attachment upload) then
  if (within the configured size cap ?) then (yes)
    :201 Attachment metadata\n(storagePath never leaves the server);
  else (no)
    :<color:#B71C1C>413 payload too large</color>;
  endif

elseif (AI assist) then
  if (AI provider available ?) then (yes)
    :200 AI suggestion, labelled AI-generated;
  else (no)
    :<color:#B71C1C>503 ai-unavailable — mapped once by</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>ProblemDetailsExceptionHandler (AP-12).</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>The rest of the screen stays live</color>;
  endif

else (create user / self-register)
  if (e-mail already taken ?) then (yes)
    :<color:#B71C1C>409 user-already-exists</color>;
  else (no)
    :201 Created + Location header;
  endif
endif

|Angular errorInterceptor|
:Every failure is normalised to a typed ApiProblem;
if (which status ?) then (401)
  :Clear the session → /auth/login?returnUrl\n(skipped for the anonymous auth endpoints);
elseif (403) then
  :Route to /403. The session is NOT cleared;
elseif (400 / 404 / 409 / 413 / 422 / 503) then
  :Passed through untouched — rendered inline,\nin context, by the screen that asked;
else (5xx / network)
  :One translated toast;
endif
:The problem is always rethrown;
stop
@enduml

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' 3. AGENT
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml USER-FLOWS-agent
title Agent — Staff Workspace lifecycle\nDepartment-scoped queue, ticket work, messaging, AI, knowledge, notifications

skinparam shadowing false
|#E8F0FE|Agent (browser)|
|#FFF4E5|API — api/v1|
|#FDEAF1|SQL Server|

|Agent (browser)|
start
:Signed in as Agent → /workspace → /workspace/queue;

partition "My queue — the landing screen (UI-2)" {
  |API — api/v1|
  :GET /tickets?assigneeId=me\n(no sort sent — the server owns urgency;\n"me" is resolved server-side, never sent as an id);
  :TicketScope: DepartmentId = the caller's department;
  |SQL Server|
  :SELECT Tickets ORDER BY\nresolutionBreached DESC, resolutionDueAt ASC;
  |Agent (browser)|
  :Table (desktop) / stacked cards (phone),\nstatus and priority chips, SLA indicator,\nquick filters kept in the URL (UI-9);
}

repeat
  if (what next ?) then (open a ticket)

    partition "Ticket detail — /workspace/tickets/:id (regions load independently)" {
      |API — api/v1|
      :GET /tickets/{id}            → header, chips, SLA due dates (frozen, A-20);
      :GET /tickets/{id}/messages   → customer-visible thread, oldest first;
      :GET /tickets/{id}/activity   → append-only history, internal entries included;
      :GET /tickets/{id}/attachments;
      :GET /tickets/{id}/suggested-articles → keyword-matched KB articles;
      :GET /customers/{id}          → customer panel (drawer at phone width);
      |Agent (browser)|
      :<color:#B71C1C>Internal notes region and ticket tasks</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>NOT IMPLEMENTED (story 14, T2-C)</color>;
    }

    if (which action on the ticket ?) then (assign / reassign)
      |API — api/v1|
      :POST /tickets/{id}/assignment {assignedUserId};
      |SQL Server|
      :UPDATE Tickets.AssignedUserId\nINSERT TicketActivity(Assigned)\nINSERT Notification(TicketAssigned);
      |Agent (browser)|
      :The status chip does NOT change (A-18);

    elseif (change status) then
      |Agent (browser)|
      :Transition menu — offers legal AND permitted only (UI-3);
      |API — api/v1|
      :POST /tickets/{id}/transition {targetStatus}\nA-16 authority first, then A-5 legality;
      |SQL Server|
      :UPDATE Tickets.Status\nINSERT TicketActivity(StatusChanged)\nINSERT AuditEntry(TicketStatusChanged);
      |Agent (browser)|
      :No optimistic UI (UI-8) — the chip moves\nonly after the server confirms;

    elseif (escalate) then
      |Agent (browser)|
      :A separate control, never inside the menu (AP-7).\nConfirmation dialog naming the effect (UI-12):\npriority rises one level, status unchanged,\na manager will be notified;
      |API — api/v1|
      :POST /tickets/{id}/escalate  (no body);
      |SQL Server|
      :UPDATE Tickets.Priority (+1; Urgent stays Urgent)\nINSERT Escalation + TicketActivity(Escalated)\nINSERT AuditEntry(TicketEscalated)\nINSERT Notification(TicketEscalated) → A-21 recipients;

    elseif (reply to the customer) then
      |Agent (browser)|
      :One composer, one Send (UI-7): quick replies from\nGET /config/staff and the AI draft both land\nin the same editable draft;
      |API — api/v1|
      :POST /tickets/{id}/messages {body}\nthe channel is the endpoint's fact, never the client's;
      |SQL Server|
      :INSERT TicketMessage(direction = Outbound)\nSET Ticket.FirstRespondedAt on the first outbound\nINSERT TicketActivity(MessagePosted);

    elseif (ask the AI panel) then
      |API — api/v1|
      :POST /tickets/{id}/ai/summary\nPOST /tickets/{id}/ai/suggested-reply\n(see USER-FLOWS-ai-kb);
      |Agent (browser)|
      :Always labelled AI-generated. "Insert into reply"\nputs text in the composer — never auto-sent (A-8);

    else (read a suggested article)
      |Agent (browser)|
      :Open → /workspace/knowledge/:id;
    endif

  elseif (create a ticket for a customer ?) then (yes)
    |Agent (browser)|
    :/workspace/tickets/new;
    |API — api/v1|
    :POST /ai/classification-suggestion (on blur)\n→ pre-selects category and priority, freely overridable;
    :POST /tickets {customerId, subject, description,\n categoryCode, priority, departmentId?}\nisUrgent, status and the SLA fields are refused (AP-10);
    |SQL Server|
    :INSERT Ticket — status New, department derived from\nthe category map (A-14), SLA due dates computed once;\nround-robin auto-assignment → Notification(TicketAssigned);
    |Agent (browser)|
    :<color:#B71C1C>Writing the AI suggestion and the agent's override</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>into ticket history: NOT IMPLEMENTED</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>(blocked by finding S9-4 — no contract field carries it)</color>;

  elseif (customers ?) then (yes)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /customers  (directory — not department-scoped)\nGET /customers/{id} + /timeline + /notes + /attachments\nPOST /customers · PATCH /customers/{id}\nPOST /customers/{id}/notes · /attachments\nGET /attachments/{id}/content (streamed download);

  elseif (knowledge base ?) then (yes)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /kb/articles?q=... — staff see internal AND public,\ninternal ones badged  ·  GET /kb/articles/{id};
    |Agent (browser)|
    :Presented as search, never as an AI answer (AP-14);

  else (notifications ?)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /notifications?unreadOnly=&paging\nPOST /notifications/{id}/read (idempotent, 204);
    |Agent (browser)|
    :Bell badge plus the /workspace/notifications list.\nNo mark-all-read control exists (AP-18);
  endif
repeat while (continue working ?) is (yes) not (no)

|Agent (browser)|
:Sign out — client-side only (AP-8);
stop
@enduml

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' 4. MANAGER
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml USER-FLOWS-manager
title Manager — everything an Agent can do, across every department

skinparam shadowing false
|#E8F0FE|Manager (browser)|
|#FFF4E5|API — api/v1|
|#FDEAF1|SQL Server|

|Manager (browser)|
start
:Signed in as Manager;
:roleRedirectGuard → /workspace → /workspace/queue\n(authentication and redirect exactly as in the master flow);

note right
  A Manager satisfies RequireAgent (A-4), so every
  Agent screen and endpoint in USER-FLOWS-agent is
  available unchanged. Only the differences are drawn here.
end note

partition "Difference 1 — scope" {
  |API — api/v1|
  :TicketScope for Manager and Administrator is\nunrestricted across departments;
  |Manager (browser)|
  :The shared department filter is ENABLED.\nAn Agent's is fixed to their own department and\ndisabled, with a hint explaining why;
}

partition "Difference 2 — escalation target" {
  |SQL Server|
  :A-21 recipient cascade on escalate and on SLA breach:\n1. the department's own Manager\n2. else every active Manager\n3. else every active Administrator;
  |Manager (browser)|
  :Notification(TicketEscalated | SlaBreached) appears\non the bell and in /workspace/notifications;
}

partition "Difference 3 — reporting" {
  :<color:#B71C1C>/workspace/reports — the management dashboard</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>(volume, SLA, per-department and per-branch aggregates):</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>**NOT IMPLEMENTED** (story 15, T2-G).</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>The nav entry is a TODO placeholder in app.menu.ts and</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>the route does not exist, so /workspace/reports falls</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>through the wildcard to /404</color>;
}

|Manager (browser)|
:Otherwise: queue, tickets, assignment, transitions,\nescalation, messaging, AI assists, knowledge,\ncustomers and notifications — as USER-FLOWS-agent;
:Sign out — client-side only (AP-8);
stop
@enduml

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' 5. ADMINISTRATOR
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml USER-FLOWS-administrator
title Administrator — Administration area (plus the whole Staff Workspace)

skinparam shadowing false
|#E8F0FE|Administrator (browser)|
|#FFF4E5|API — api/v1|
|#FDEAF1|SQL Server|

|Administrator (browser)|
start
:Signed in as Administrator → /workspace/queue\n(an Administrator satisfies the Agent guard, A-4);
:The sidebar shows BOTH sections:\nWorkspace (as USER-FLOWS-agent) and Administration;

repeat
  if (which administration task ?) then (users — T1-D)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /users?role=&departmentId=&q=&paging → directory;
    :GET /users/{id} → detail;
    split
      :Create a staff user;
      |API — api/v1|
      :POST /users {email, password, displayName,\n role, departmentId, branchId}\nrole = Customer is rejected (DM-1);
      |SQL Server|
      :INSERT Users + AuditEntry(UserCreated);\n409 user-already-exists on a duplicate e-mail;
    split again
      :Edit role / department / branch / display name;
      |API — api/v1|
      :PATCH /users/{id};
      |SQL Server|
      :UPDATE Users\nINSERT AuditEntry(UserRoleChanged |\nUserDepartmentChanged | UserEmailChanged);
      |Administrator (browser)|
      :Takes effect on the target's VERY NEXT request —\nthe token carries no role claim (AD-15);
    split again
      :Deactivate (confirmation dialog, UI-12);
      |API — api/v1|
      :POST /users/{id}/deactivate → 204;
      |SQL Server|
      :UPDATE Users.IsActive = 0\nINSERT AuditEntry(UserDeactivated);
      |Administrator (browser)|
      :That user's next request is 401, whatever their\ntoken says. A user is never deleted;
    end split

  elseif (audit log — T2-H) then (yes)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /audit?actorUserId=&action=&from=&to=&paging\nAdministrator-only, newest first;
    |SQL Server|
    :SELECT AuditEntries — append-only, written by\nAuditRecorder from Application services:\nSignInSucceeded, SignInFailed, UserCreated,\nUserDeactivated, UserRoleChanged,\nUserDepartmentChanged, UserEmailChanged,\nTicketStatusChanged, TicketEscalated;
    |Administrator (browser)|
    :Read-only screen. No export and no delete;

  elseif (configuration — T2-I) then (yes)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /config/staff — priorities, quick replies,\nSLA targets, category → department map;\nGET /config — categories, feedback scale;
    |Administrator (browser)|
    :Read-only effective configuration. Editing is by\nappsettings / environment only — there is no write\nendpoint, by design;

  elseif (knowledge authoring — T2-E) then (yes)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET   /kb/articles                → authoring list\nPOST  /kb/articles                → create (draft by default)\nPATCH /kb/articles/{id}           → title, body, type, visibility\nPOST  /kb/articles/{id}/publish   → publish\nPOST  /kb/articles/{id}/unpublish → unpublish;
    |SQL Server|
    :INSERT / UPDATE KnowledgeArticles — the author is the\nauthenticated Administrator, never accepted from a client;
    |Administrator (browser)|
    :<color:#B71C1C>Delete an article, and version history:</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>NOT IMPLEMENTED — no route, no endpoint (T2-E)</color>;

  else (platform health)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /health → the /status screen (Administrator-only),\nthe only screen that reports database connectivity;
  endif
repeat while (more administration ?) is (yes) not (no)

|Administrator (browser)|
:Sign out — client-side only (AP-8);
stop
@enduml

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' 6. CUSTOMER
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml USER-FLOWS-customer
title Customer — Customer Portal self-service lifecycle

skinparam shadowing false
|#E8F0FE|Customer (browser)|
|#FFF4E5|API — api/v1|
|#FDEAF1|SQL Server|

|Customer (browser)|
start
if (has an account ?) then (no)
  :/auth/register — self-registration;
  |API — api/v1|
  :POST /auth/register  «anonymous»;
  |SQL Server|
  :INSERT Users(role = Customer) + Customers\non the configured default branch (A-15);
  |API — api/v1|
  :201 AuthToken — signed in immediately;
else (yes)
  :/auth/login → POST /auth/login → 200 AuthToken;
endif

|Customer (browser)|
:roleRedirectGuard → /portal (PortalShell)\n→ /portal/requests/new;
note right
  A Customer is not "at least an Agent", so no staff
  screen is ever loaded — /workspace and /admin are
  separate lazy chunks behind their own guards (AD-14),
  and their endpoints answer 403 regardless.
  Portal navigation today: Submit a request · Help.
end note

repeat
  if (what next ?) then (submit a request — T2-B)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /config → categories (code and name only —\nthe category → department map is staff-only, AP-17)\nand the feedback rating scale;
    |Customer (browser)|
    :Exactly four inputs (ui-design §7.2): subject,\ndescription, category, and a "this is urgent" checkbox —\nan indication, never a priority (A-17).\nNo department, no priority, no SLA wording (UI-11);
    |API — api/v1|
    :POST /portal/tickets\nAuthenticated submission only (A-9);
    |SQL Server|
    :INSERT Ticket — status New, department derived from\nthe category (A-14), priority server-derived, SLA due\ndates computed once and frozen (A-20);\nround-robin auto-assignment → Notification(TicketAssigned);
    |Customer (browser)|
    :201 → navigate to /portal/requests/{id};

  elseif (read or reply to a request ?) then (yes)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /portal/tickets/{id}/messages\nAnother customer's ticket → 404 (AP-4).\nInternal notes are unreachable by path (AP-5);
    |Customer (browser)|
    :Thread plus reply composer. Channel and author role\nare omitted from the portal payload (UI-11).\nNothing polls — this is not chat (T3-B);
    |API — api/v1|
    :POST /portal/tickets/{id}/messages {body};
    |SQL Server|
    :INSERT TicketMessage(direction = Inbound, channel = Portal)\nINSERT TicketActivity(MessagePosted)\nINSERT Notification(CustomerReplied) → staff;
    if (what was the status ?) then (Pending)
      |SQL Server|
      :UPDATE Tickets.Status = Open in the SAME transaction\nINSERT TicketActivity(StatusChanged), attributed to\nthe replying customer (R-13, R-14);
      |Customer (browser)|
      :The response envelope {message, ticketStatus, statusChanged}\ndrives the "reopened" cue in place — no re-fetch, no guess;
    elseif (Closed or Cancelled) then
      :<color:#B71C1C>409 ticket-terminal (A-5)</color>;
    else (New / Open / Resolved)
      :Status unchanged. A reply never reopens a Resolved\nrequest — that is the explicit transition A-16 grants,\nand its control is story 13's;
    endif

  elseif (help centre — T2-E) then (yes)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /portal/kb/articles?q=...\nGET /portal/kb/articles/{id};
    |SQL Server|
    :SELECT KnowledgeArticles WHERE IsPublished = 1\nAND Visibility = Public (constraint 19).\nAn internal or unpublished id → 404;
    |Customer (browser)|
    :Self-service search and article reader\n(/portal/help and /portal/help/:id);

  else (nothing else exists yet)
    :<color:#B71C1C>NOT IMPLEMENTED for a Customer today (story 13, T2-F):</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>· /portal/requests — the "My requests" list</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>  (/portal lands on requests/new instead)</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>· Cancel-own-request and reopen-resolved controls —</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>  the A-16 authority exists server-side, no UI calls it</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>· Portal attachments, and the satisfaction / feedback control</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>· A customer notification feed — excluded by design:</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>  A-13's four notification types are staff-facing</color>;
  endif
repeat while (continue ?) is (yes) not (no)

|Customer (browser)|
:Sign out — client-side only (AP-8);
stop
@enduml

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' 7. TICKET LIFECYCLE — a UML state machine (A-5 legality x A-16 authority)
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml USER-FLOWS-ticket-state
title Ticket lifecycle — the A-5 state machine with A-16 authority\n(TicketLifecycle.Legal + TransitionAuthority.MayInvoke)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #33475B
  FontColor #22303F
}

[*] --> New : POST /tickets (agent, on behalf of a customer)\nPOST /portal/tickets (customer web form)\nstatus, department and SLA dates are server-derived

state New
state Open
state Pending
state Resolved
state Closed #EEEEEE
state Cancelled #EEEEEE

New --> Open : staff
New --> Cancelled : staff, or the owning customer\n(A-16 + A-18: only while still New)

Open --> Pending : staff
Open --> Resolved : staff
Open --> Cancelled : staff

Pending --> Open : staff
Pending --> Open : AUTOMATIC — the owning customer posts a reply\nPOST /portal/tickets/{id}/messages (R-13),\nsame transaction, attributed to the customer (R-14)
Pending --> Resolved : staff
Pending --> Cancelled : staff

Resolved --> Open : staff, or the owning customer (reopen own)\ncustomer control NOT IMPLEMENTED (story 13)
Resolved --> Closed : staff only — a customer may never close
Resolved --> Cancelled : staff

Closed --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]

note right of Closed
  Terminal: no outgoing edge at all.
  A ticket is cancelled, never deleted.
  There is no timer and no automatic closure anywhere.
end note

note left of New
  **Escalation is an action, not a transition** (AP-7, A-5).
  POST /tickets/{id}/escalate raises the priority exactly one
  level (Urgent stays Urgent) and leaves the status where it is,
  from any non-terminal state. Staff only.
  It also fires from the SLA sweep — see USER-FLOWS-sla.
end note

note bottom
  **Three independent refusals, deliberately distinguishable** (api-design §5.6)
  · 404 — the ticket is outside the caller's scope (TicketScope, AP-4)
  · 403 transition-not-permitted — the edge exists, the caller may not invoke it (A-16)
  · 409 illegal-transition — the edge is not in this graph (A-5); the problem detail
    carries allowedTransitions (finding F-1: it is not on the ticket payload)
  The client mirrors the matrix in shared/lifecycle/transition-matrix.ts to decide
  what to OFFER; the server decides what is ALLOWED.
end note
@enduml

'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' 8. SLA, ESCALATION AND NOTIFICATIONS — the flow that does not start in a browser
'------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml USER-FLOWS-sla
title SLA monitoring, escalation and notifications\nThe flow that does not start in the browser (AD-6, A-3, A-13, A-21)

skinparam shadowing false
|#FFF4E5|SlaMonitorHostedService (in-process timer)|
|#FFE9D6|Application services|
|#FDEAF1|SQL Server|
|#E8F0FE|Staff browser|

|SlaMonitorHostedService (in-process timer)|
start
:Host starts → one sweep immediately, then every\nSweepIntervalSeconds (PeriodicTimer).\nNo queue, no broker, no external scheduler;
repeat
  :Create a DI scope; set the SYSTEM identity;
  |Application services|
  :SlaEvaluationService.EvaluateDueTicketsAsync;
  |SQL Server|
  :SELECT Tickets WHERE the status is not terminal AND\n( (FirstResponseDueAt <= now AND NOT FirstResponseBreached\n    AND FirstRespondedAt IS NULL)\n  OR (ResolutionDueAt <= now AND NOT ResolutionBreached\n    AND ResolvedAt IS NULL) )\n— served by the two filtered indexes;
  if (any tickets due ?) then (yes)
    |Application services|
    :Latch the breach flag(s) — idempotent by construction:\nthe flags this pass sets are in the next pass's predicate;
    :Escalate through TicketLifecycleService.EscalateAsync\n(actor = System) — the SAME path the manual button uses,\nnot a second implementation;
    :Resolve recipients via IEscalationRecipientPolicy (A-21):\nthe department's manager, else all Managers,\nelse all Administrators;
    |SQL Server|
    :UPDATE Tickets (breach flags, priority +1)\nINSERT TicketActivity(Escalated)\nINSERT AuditEntry(TicketEscalated)\nINSERT Notification(SlaBreached, TicketEscalated)\nCOMMITTED ONCE for the whole sweep;
  else (no)
    |Application services|
    :Nothing to do;
  endif
repeat while (host running ?) is (yes) not (shutdown)
|SlaMonitorHostedService (in-process timer)|
:A failed tick is logged and the loop continues;
stop

|Staff browser|
partition "How a notification reaches a person" {
  :Every navigation calls NotificationStore.refresh()\n— staff only, skipped for a Customer session;
  :GET /notifications?pageSize=10 → bell badge and panel;
  :Opening one marks it read:\nPOST /notifications/{id}/read (204, idempotent).\nNo optimistic decrement (UI-8); no mark-all-read (AP-18);
  :The full list is at /workspace/notifications;
}

note right
  **The four notification types (A-13), and no others**
  · TicketAssigned  — manual assignment, or round-robin
  · SlaBreached     — raised by the sweep, the only system actor
  · TicketEscalated — manual escalate, or the sweep
  · CustomerReplied — a customer posted on the portal

  **Known simplification, reported not fixed (A-3, PF-5):**
  the clock is 24/7 wall-clock from createdAt — no business hours,
  no holidays, and Pending does NOT pause it. A ticket resolved
  without an outbound reply stays first-response breached.

  **NOT IMPLEMENTED:** e-mail, SMS or push delivery. A notification
  is a database row read by the in-app bell — nothing else.
end note
@enduml

